Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:18:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/37] replay0905-v0159.2: re-pin upstream identity to
 rust-v0.159.2

Baseline identity bump (UPSTREAM_UPGRADE.md checklist item 1) so the
tree no longer declares a base it is not built from. The Go-side
readiness gate cross-checks codex_tag / codex_commit /
cargo_lock_sha256 from /info, so a stale constant here is a live
correctness bug, not a doc nit.

  tag          rust-v0.159.0 -> rust-v0.159.2
  tag object   377f7f557a6bdea0f3a2d26d4d899c66db4789d0 -> 8b9fa496bbf2c47aebd62e85a080b9a522a455b5
  commit       687a119f0fcaace47e1f1abcc77cec6c813fd6da -> ff6aec96948b70d94983af2641a6b67c94faeff5
  base tree    bee1375c8502e4c4d71db017f7e087dfbb3e775c -> 406dfdd5c68f303a3a8d04f32b3965b3b0ca0361
  Cargo.lock   16b915e94730a7e598182620923fc6eae19e32366d3b5ef91128002575ae24af
               -> 4fab6fe99180e2b8f305bd4b33c1b4bd825e3fa4cdef1045be750843bd3d431e

MODULE.bazel.lock and the v8 pin (150.4.0) are byte-identical between
the two bases, so those digests are unchanged.

Also bumps the version-derived golden fixture: the operation snapshot
generator string is env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION"), which follows the
workspace version, so tests/fixtures/operations_snapshot.golden.json
must move to v0.159.2 with it.
